# =============================================================================
# RETIRED — image CVE suppression is no longer supported (bugfix 2.8).
# =============================================================================
# This file is NO LONGER CONSUMED. .github/workflows/deploy.yml and
# .github/workflows/_docker.yml previously passed it to `trivy image` as
# `--ignorefile ci/trivyignore.images`, alongside `--ignore-unfixed`
# (Trivy) / `--only-fixed` (Grype). Task 3.18 (ci-pipeline-remediation)
# removed all four: the zero High/Critical policy blocks on every resolved
# finding regardless of fix availability, prior count, or suppression text —
# there is no longer an exception path for image CVEs, mirroring the
# dependency-scan policy in ci/trivyignore's software-CVE-free namespace.
#
# A HIGH/CRITICAL image finding must now be remediated (base image digest
# bump, OS/application package upgrade, or package removal) — see
# backend/Dockerfile and frontend/Dockerfile, and
# backend/tools/ci/pin_authority.py for the current digest pins.
#
# This file is kept only so a stale reference to it (docs, old branches)
# resolves to an explanation rather than a 404. It is safe to delete once no
# workflow or doc references it.
# =============================================================================
